      "name": "InitializeDirectSound",
      "signature": "void InitializeDirectSound(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize DirectSound audio subsystem with optional 3D and EAX support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if already initialized or disabled\n2. Create critical section to protect audio initialization\n3. Call DirectSoundCreate to create primary audio device\n4. If successful, configure primary buffer format (22050 Hz, 16-bit stereo)\n5. Create secondary sound buffer for audio playback\n6. Load 3D listener object if 3D support enabled\n7. Attempt EAX initialization (EAX 1.0 or EAX 2.0)\n8. Set primary buffer effects and listener orientation\n9. Start audio playback and log initialization status\n10. On error, clean up allocated resources and log failure\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains module context\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f3c80 enables 3D sound support flag\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9f3c7c enables enhanced audio flag\n\nReturns:\n- void (initializes global audio state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initializes only once (checked via DAT_6f9f3c8c flag)\n- Supports DirectSound3D for positional audio\n- Supports optional EAX effects\n- Logs all DirectSound errors with descriptive messages\n- Cleans up all COM objects on initialization failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
