      "name": "ShutdownSoundSystem",
      "signature": "void ShutdownSoundSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Shutdown and cleanup function that deallocates all slots and pool memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system is initialized (g_dwInitialized)\n2. Acquire critical section lock (g_hSlotMutex)\n3. Call CloseSoundStream on each slot in g_adSlotData (cleanup phase 1)\n4. Call CloseSoundObject on each slot and zero the array (cleanup phase 2)\n5. Iterate through linked list at g_pCacheListHead:\n   - Read next pointer from offset 0x5c before freeing\n   - If offset 0x50 is non-zero, call ReleasePoolAllocation (pool 0x67)\n   - Call ReleasePoolAllocation (pool 0x68) for each node\n6. Zero g_dwInitialized flag and delete critical section\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwInitialized (uint): Initialization flag\n- IMPLICIT: g_hSlotMutex: Critical section for synchronization\n- IMPLICIT: g_adSlotData (uint[]): Array of slot pointers\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6f9f3cc8: End of g_adSlotData array (loop bounds)\n- 0x50: Offset to conditional field in linked list node\n- 0x5c: Offset to next pointer in linked list node\n- 0x67: Pool ID for secondary allocation\n- 0x68: Pool ID for primary node allocation\n\nNotes:\n- nTemp1 is a decompiler artifact (HASH-based storage) storing next pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
