      "name": "HasAnySoundBufferActive",
      "signature": "int HasAnySoundBufferActive(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if any sound slot has an active sound buffer.\n\nExported as Ordinal_10040 - Public API for sound system state query.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if sound system initialized (g_dwInitialized != 0)\n2. If not initialized, return 0 (no active buffers)\n3. Iterate through g_adSlotData array (8 slots, 32 bytes total)\n4. For each slot, call GetSampleSoundBuffer (Ordinal_10013)\n5. If any slot returns non-zero (has active buffer), return 1\n6. After checking all slots, return 0 (no active buffers)\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: At least one sound slot has an active buffer\n- 0: No active buffers or sound system not initialized\n\nGlobal State:\n- g_dwInitialized (0x6f9f3ce0): Sound system initialization flag\n- g_adSlotData (0x6f9f3ca8): Array of 8 sound slot pointers\n\nLoop Analysis:\n- Counter: ESI (pointer)\n- Bounds: [0x6f9f3ca8, 0x6f9f3cc8)\n- Stride: 4 bytes (pointer size)\n- Trip count: 8 iterations ((0x6f9f3cc8 - 0x6f9f3ca8) / 4)",
