      "name": "SAudCloseStreamAndCleanup",
      "signature": "int SAudCloseStreamAndCleanup(int * pSoundObj)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes audio stream and releases associated resources under critical section protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate non-null pSoundObj parameter\n2. Enter critical section to protect shared state\n3. Call virtual method at offset 0x24 to initiate closure\n4. Exit if operation fails (return value < 0)\n5. Check byClosureFlags (bits from closure flags structure)\n6. If bit 2 set, wait for pending operations (offset 0x50) with Sleep(10) retry on WAIT_TIMEOUT\n7. Close audio stream (pSoundObj[0x12]) and file handle if closure completed\n8. Clear stream pointer and internal state fields\n9. Leave critical section and return success\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundObj (int*): Pointer to sound object structure containing vtable, stream handle at [0x12], flags at [7]\n- IMPLICIT: byClosureFlags contains mode bits from closure operation result\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Successful closure and cleanup\n- 0: Closure failed or error during operation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24: Virtual method offset for initiating closure\n- 0x48: Virtual method offset for resource cleanup\n- 0x50: Virtual method offset for polling pending operations\n- 0x7787ff6a: WAIT_TIMEOUT error code for retry loop\n- 0x12: Array offset for stream handle pointer\n- 0x1c: Array offset for internal state field to clear",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
