      "name": "InitializeGameObjectState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameObjectState(uint * pObject, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a game object's audio state by configuring sound buffer properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse flags to determine mono (bit 0) or stereo (bit 1) audio mode\n2. Calculate sample rate: 0x40000 for stereo, 0x20000 for mono\n3. Initialize wave format structure via InitializeWaveFormat\n4. Retrieve game audio subsystem state via GetGameState\n5. Create sound buffer through COM vtable call (offset +0xC)\n6. If stereo mode requested:\n   a. Query primary buffer interface (IID at 0x6f9ee214)\n   b. Check system error state via GetLastError\n   c. Query secondary buffer interface (IID at 0x6f9ee204)\n   d. Determine audio capability level (1=basic, other=enhanced)\n   e. Set audio format based on capability level\n   f. Verify format acceptance (flags & 0x3 == 0x3)\n7. Store calculated values in object structure:\n   - Offset +0x04: Sample rate\n   - Offset +0x08: Half sample rate\n   - Offset +0x30: State index (initialized to -1)\n   - Offset +0x34: Original flags\n\nParameters:\n  pObject (ECX) - Pointer to game object structure to initialize\n  dwFlags (EDX) - Configuration flags:\n                  Bit 0 (0x1): Mono audio mode\n                  Bit 1 (0x2): Stereo audio mode\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) - Object successfully initialized\n  0 (FALSE) - Initialization failed (COM call failed, format rejected)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If neither mono nor stereo bit set, defaults to mono configuration\n  - Format validation requires (result & 0x3) == 0x3 for success\n  - On any COM failure, releases acquired interfaces before returning\n\nError Handling:\n  - Negative HRESULT from COM calls triggers early exit with cleanup\n  - GetLastError checked to determine system audio state\n  - All acquired COM interfaces are released on failure paths\n\nStructure Layout (Object at pObject):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    4     ppvVtable     void**  COM vtable pointer\n  0x04    4     dwSampleRate  uint    Calculated sample rate\n  0x08    4     dwHalfRate    uint    Sample rate / 2\n  0x0C    4     pPrimary      void*   Primary buffer interface\n  0x10    4     pSecondary    void*   Secondary buffer interface\n  0x30    4     nStateIndex   int     State index (-1 = uninitialized)\n  0x34    4     dwOrigFlags   uint    Original initialization flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20000  - Base sample rate for mono audio\n  0x40000  - Base sample rate for stereo audio\n  0xE0     - Channel configuration for mono (224)\n  0xD4     - Channel configuration adjustment for stereo (-44)\n  0x6f9ee214 - IID for primary DirectSound buffer interface\n  0x6f9ee204 - IID for secondary DirectSound buffer interface",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:eacbf1bb6fb436dd3e9fa201d7d4232edafc677ddabfdec2051a0fa51e160f5a",
