      "name": "CloseSoundObject",
      "signature": "void CloseSoundObject(void * pSound)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Closes and deallocates a sound object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not NULL\n2. Lock critical section for thread-safe access\n3. Close stream if active (SAudCloseStream)\n4. Call virtual destructor through vtable\n5. Close file handle if open\n6. Release all associated memory structures\n7. Zero out entire structure (24 dwords = 96 bytes)\n8. Release pool allocation for the object\n\nParameters:\n- pSound (void*): Pointer to sound object structure (96 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds or asserts)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12 (18): Offset of stream handle field\n- 0x48: Offset of virtual destructor in vtable\n- 0x18 (24): Loop count for clearing structure\n- 8: Offset of virtual destructor in derived vtables",
