      "name": "FadeVolumeOverDuration",
      "signature": "undefined FadeVolumeOverDuration(uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Gradually fades sound volume to zero over a specified duration.\nOrdinal: 10029\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is active; return immediately if not\n2. Assert dwDuration > 0 (exit with error if invalid)\n3. Get current volume factor from global; calculate step decrement\n4. Enter fade loop: sleep 20ms per iteration\n5. Decrement volume by step each iteration (clamp to 0)\n6. Re-check game state each iteration; skip update if game stopped\n7. Validate volume in range [0, 255] before applying\n8. Enter critical section to protect sound sample list\n9. Update global volume factor\n10. Iterate through linked list of active sound samples\n11. For each sample: validate ptSample not null and has sound buffer\n12. Calculate new volume: (globalVolume * sampleVolume) / 255\n13. Check sample flags (bit 2) and global flag for attenuation mode\n14. Apply sound mute override if g_dwSoundMute is set\n15. Call CalculateSoundAttenuation to compute final attenuation\n16. Call DirectSound SetVolume via vtable offset 0x3c\n17. Leave critical section after processing all samples\n18. Continue loop until volume reaches zero\n\nParameters:\ndwDuration (ECX) - Fade duration in milliseconds; must be > 0. Divided by 20ms to determine iteration count.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns immediately if game state is inactive\n- Asserts and exits if dwDuration <= 0\n- Asserts and exits if calculated volume outside [0, 255]\n- Asserts and exits if sample pointer or sound buffer is null\n- Volume is clamped to 0 when step exceeds remaining volume\n- Sound mute flag (g_dwSoundMute) forces volume to 0\n\nGlobals Used:\ng_dwVolumeFactor - Current master volume level (0-255)\ng_hSoundCriticalSection - Protects sound sample list access\ng_pSampleListHead - Head of linked list of active sound samples\ng_dwSoundMute - Mute override flag (non-zero = muted)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 (20) - Sleep interval in milliseconds per fade step\n0xFF (255) - Maximum volume value\n0x3c (60) - VTable offset for IDirectSoundBuffer::SetVolume\n0x0e (14) - Sample structure offset for individual volume\n0x0d (13) - Sample structure offset for flags byte\n0x04 - Flag bit mask for attenuation mode check",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:82027df527ed8a09f875861b1dfdef0f",
