      "name": "UpdateSoundVolumeThread",
      "signature": "void UpdateSoundVolumeThread(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Background thread that gradually adjusts master volume for all active sound samples.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate volume step size from current settings\n2. Loop until target volume (EBX=0) is reached\n3. Sleep 20ms between iterations for smooth volume transition\n4. Verify game state is active before processing\n5. Validate volume is within range [0, 255]\n6. Enter critical section for thread-safe sample list access\n7. Update global volume factor (g_dwVolumeFactor)\n8. Iterate through linked list of sound samples (g_pSampleListHead)\n9. For each sample, calculate scaled volume from base volume at offset 0x38\n10. Apply attenuation flags check (byte at offset 0x34, bit 2)\n11. If muted (g_dwSoundMute != 0), set volume to 0\n12. Calculate final attenuation via CalculateSoundAttenuation\n13. Apply volume to DirectSound buffer via vtable call at offset 0x3c\n14. Leave critical section and continue loop\n\nParameters: None (thread entry point with no arguments)\n\nReturns: void (infinite loop, does not return normally)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if sample pointer is NULL (line 0x2D8)\n- Asserts if sample buffer pointer is NULL (line 0x2BF)\n- Asserts if volume out of range [0, 255] (line 0x3AD)\n- Calls ReportError(-1) on assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x14 (20): Sleep duration in milliseconds\n- 0xFF (255): Maximum volume value\n- 0x80808081: Magic constant for division by 255 optimization\n- 0x437f0000: Float constant 255.0 for CalculateSoundAttenuation\n\nStructure Layout (SoundSample at pSample):\nOffset  Size  Field               Description\n0x00    4     pDirectSoundBuffer  Pointer to DirectSound buffer (vtable)\n0x34    1     bFlags              Sound flags (bit 2 = attenuation check)\n0x38    4     dwBaseVolume        Base volume level for this sample\n0x3c    4     flAttenuation       Attenuation factor (float)\n\nGlobals:\n- g_dwVolumeFactor (0x6f9f063c): Current master volume [0-255]\n- g_pSampleListHead (0x6f9f3d00): Head of linked list of active samples\n- g_dwSoundMute (0x6f9f3d0c): Mute flag (non-zero = muted)\n- lpCriticalSection (0x6f9f3c50): Thread synchronization object",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:fe80ad123195640c6f02a6d6a897f8bceb48a71bc9b67125f62393846f1393c3",
