      "name": "OpenAudioStream",
      "signature": "dword OpenAudioStream(void * this, int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Opens an audio stream from an async file handle with specified parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input context pointer (pSoundContext must not be null)\n2. Get async file handle via SetAsyncFileHandle\n3. Enter critical section for thread-safe operations\n4. Open audio stream via SAudOpenAudioStreamEx with parameters\n5. Handle looping flag by converting to 0x40000 flag bit\n6. Store file handle in context[0x48] and set state flags\n7. Leave critical section and return success\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundContext (void*): Audio context structure pointer\n- nSampleRate (int): Sample rate multiplier (multiplied by 4 for buffer)\n- nLooping (int): Looping control (0=no loop, non-zero=loop enabled)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 on failure (assertion on null context)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
