      "name": "IsAudioObjectValid",
      "signature": "int IsAudioObjectValid(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if the global audio game object is initialized and in a valid state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pAudioGameObject is non-NULL\n2. If NULL, return 0 (invalid)\n3. Call IsStateValid() to validate internal state\n4. Return 1 if valid, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_pAudioGameObject (void*) - Global audio object pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if audio object exists and is valid\n- 0 if audio object is NULL or in invalid state",
