      "name": "ParseWavFile",
      "signature": "int * ParseWavFile(int * pWavBuffer, uint * pdwBytesRemaining, ushort * pWavFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Parses a WAV file header and extracts format information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify RIFF header (0x46464952) and WAVE format (0x45564157)\n2. Scan for fmt chunk (0x20746d66) in the WAV structure\n3. Validate chunk sizes against remaining buffer length\n4. Extract format data into pWavFormat output buffer\n5. Scan for data chunk (0x61746164) to locate sample data\n6. Return pointer to audio sample data on success\n\nParameters:\n- pWavBuffer (int*): Pointer to WAV file buffer in memory\n- pdwBytesRemaining (uint*): Pointer to remaining byte count; updated as chunks are consumed\n- pWavFormat (ushort*): Output buffer for WAV format data (channels, sample rate, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to audio data chunk on success\n- NULL on parse error (invalid header, malformed chunks, insufficient space)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x46464952: \"RIFF\" header magic\n- 0x45564157: \"WAVE\" format magic\n- 0x20746d66: \"fmt \" chunk identifier\n- 0x61746164: \"data\" chunk identifier\n- 0x10: Minimum fmt chunk size (16 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
