      "name": "ConvertColorComponentsToByteValues",
      "signature": "void ConvertColorComponentsToByteValues(int * pdwComponent1, int * pdwComponent2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts floating-point color components to clamped byte values (0-255 range).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6f9e5b10() to prepare floating-point values on FPU stack\n2. Convert first component to integer, clamp to [0, 255]\n3. Convert second component to integer, clamp to [0, 255]\n4. Store clamped values to output parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pdwComponent1 (int*): Output for first color component (0-255)\n- pdwComponent2 (int*): Output for second color component (0-255)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Uses FPU for floating-point computation\n- __ftol() converts ST(0) to integer\n- Clamping enforces byte range [0, 255]",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
