      "name": "CleanupFileResources",
      "signature": "void CleanupFileResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup file mapping and handle resources on exception/error path.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Capture current error code via GetLastError()\n2. Close mapped view if pointer at [EBP-0x20] is valid (non-NULL, checked via EBX comparison)\n3. Close file handle if handle at [EBP-0x40] is valid (non-NULL, checked via EBX comparison)\n4. Close file mapping handle EDI if not INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (-1)\n5. Restore original error code via SetLastError()\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains base register (used as NULL check comparand)\n- IMPLICIT: EBP contains stack frame base (for local variable access)\n- IMPLICIT: EDI contains file mapping handle\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds, restores error context)\n\nNotes:\n- Called from exception handler path in ReadFileIntoBuffer\n- Preserves error code to avoid masking original failure\n- Handles NULL pointers gracefully via CMP/JZ pattern\n- EDI checked for INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE before close",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5616e238127d4fc0980aa36d84ddf0bd758da7251a5cb91b3d22fec8ad05eca0",
