      "name": "CheckFloatingPointModulus",
      "signature": "undefined4 CheckFloatingPointModulus(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Checks if the modulus operation result is less than pi constant\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dividend value from g_dDividend (0x100282c8)\n2. Load divisor value from g_dDivisor (0x100282d0) \n3. Calculate floating point modulus: remainder = dividend - (dividend / divisor) * divisor\n4. Compare remainder with g_dPiConstant (pi value)\n5. Return 1 if remainder < pi, otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\n    None\n\nReturns:\n    1 (true) if floating point modulus is less than pi constant\n    0 (false) if floating point modulus is greater than or equal to pi constant\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    Uses floating point arithmetic for modulus calculation instead of integer operation\n    Compares result against mathematical pi constant for threshold decision\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    g_dPiConstant @ 0x10027ce8 - Mathematical pi constant (3.14159...)\n    g_dDividend @ 0x100282c8 - Global dividend for modulus calculation  \n    g_dDivisor @ 0x100282d0 - Global divisor for modulus calculation\n\nAlgorithm Step Mapping:\n    Step 1-2: FLD instructions at 0x1001ddfd and 0x1001de06\n    Step 3: FDIV, FMUL, FSUBR sequence at 0x1001de12-0x1001de18\n    Step 4: FCOMP instruction at 0x1001de21\n    Step 5: Conditional jump at 0x1001de2a based on comparison flags\n\nError Handling:\n    No explicit error handling - assumes valid floating point operands\n    Relies on FPU flag handling for comparison results\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporary variables optimized away by decompiler",
