      "name": "ClearFloatValue",
      "signature": "float10 ClearFloatValue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10",
      "comment": "Clears floating-point value and returns extended precision zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Discard current value on FPU stack (FSTP ST0)\n2. Load extended precision zero onto FPU stack (FLDZ)\n3. Return the zero value in ST0 register\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nfloat10 - Always returns extended precision zero (0.0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction operates on x87 FPU stack, discarding any existing value before returning zero.\nUsed to reset or initialize floating-point calculations.",
