      "name": "ComputeReducedPowerDamageWithFPUSetup",
      "signature": "void ComputeReducedPowerDamageWithFPUSetup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "High-precision FPU wrapper for power-based damage calculation.\n\nThis wrapper function prepares the floating-point stack and calls ComputePowerDouble\nfor IEEE 754 compliant damage calculations. Only invoked when FPU validation passes\nin the dispatcher (all control/exception mask bits set).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save frame pointer and establish stack frame\n2. Allocate 16 bytes of stack space for double-precision storage\n3. Align stack pointer to 16-byte boundary for SSE compatibility\n4. Exchange ST0 and ST1 FPU registers to correct parameter order\n5. Store ST1 (baseValue) as double to [ESP+0]\n6. Store ST0 (exponent) as double to [ESP+8]\n7. Call ComputePowerDouble with prepared double parameters\n8. Restore stack frame and return\n\nParameters:\n- baseValue (double in ST1): Base damage value for power calculation\n- exponent (double in ST0): Power exponent value\n\nReturns:\n- void: Result returned via FPU ST0 register from ComputePowerDouble\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only called when g_dwFPUControlWord is non-zero (optimization enabled)\n- Requires FPU control word bits 0-6 = 0x7f (precision/rounding enabled)\n- Requires MXCSR bits 12-18 = 0x1f80 (SSE exception masks all set)\n- FPU registers ST0/ST1 swapped before storing to correct parameter order\n- Stack aligned to 16-byte boundary per x86 ABI requirements\n\nRelated Functions:\n- DispatchDamageCalculationByFPUState: Dispatcher that validates FPU state\n- ComputePowerDouble: Core power calculation with double precision\n- ComputeLogarithmWithExceptionHandling: Alternative path if validation fails",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
