      "name": "ConstructExtendedFloat",
      "signature": "float10 * ConstructExtendedFloat(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, double dMantissa)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Constructs an 80-bit extended precision floating point value from IEEE 754 double precision mantissa and exponent bias.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load double precision mantissa from parameter dMantissa\n2. Extract exponent bias from nExponentBias parameter (typically +0x3fe for double to extended conversion)\n3. Add exponent bias (0x3fe) to input bias to create extended precision exponent\n4. Mask mantissa bits using AND 0x800f to preserve sign and low mantissa bits\n5. Shift adjusted exponent left by 4 bits to align with extended precision format\n6. OR exponent with masked mantissa bits to construct final extended precision value\n7. Store result in temporary double precision storage and reload for extended precision return\n\nParameters:\n- __return_storage_ptr__: Pointer to memory location for storing 80-bit extended precision result\n- dMantissa: IEEE 754 double precision mantissa (64-bit)\n- nExponentBias: Signed 16-bit exponent bias adjustment value\n\nReturns:\n- float10*: Pointer to constructed 80-bit extended precision floating point value\n- Returns constructed value by loading from temporary storage area\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses 0x3fe bias constant (1022 decimal) for IEEE 754 double to extended precision conversion\n- Mask 0x800f preserves sign bit (0x8000) and low 4 mantissa bits (0x000f)\n- Extended precision format: 1 sign + 15 exponent + 64 mantissa bits\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x3fe: IEEE 754 double precision exponent bias (1022 decimal)\n- 0x800f: Bit mask for sign and low mantissa preservation\n- 0x4: Left shift count to align exponent in extended precision format",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
