      "name": "SetSingleLocale",
      "signature": "undefined4 SetSingleLocale(int param_1, uint * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Sets a locale for a single locale category (codec) at the specified index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse locale parameter string into locale components via ParseLocaleString\n2. Allocate memory for the new locale string copy\n3. Back up existing codec data (locale string, codec value, code page)\n4. Set new locale string and copy parsed locale info to codec table\n5. Update global code page if codec index is LC_CTYPE(2) or LC_COLLATE(1)\n6. Call codec initialization callback; on failure, restore backup\n7. On success, free old locale string if not default; return new locale string\n\nParameters:\n  nCodecIndex - Locale category index (0-5, maps to LC_* constants)\n  lpszLocaleParam - Locale string to parse and set (e.g., \"en_US.UTF-8\")\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to new locale string on success, NULL on failure\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns NULL if ParseLocaleString fails to parse input\n  - Returns NULL if memory allocation fails\n  - Restores previous locale on codec init callback failure\n\nGlobal State:\n  - Updates g_dwLcTypeCodePage (0x4136cc) when nCodecIndex == 2\n  - Updates g_dwLcCollateCodePage (0x4136d0) when nCodecIndex == 1\n  - Modifies locale data table at 0x4129dc (stride 12)\n  - Modifies code page table at 0x4136b4 (stride 4)\n  - Modifies locale info table at 0x413708 (stride 6)\n\nNote: abCodecDataBackup type cannot be resolved via MCP (Ghidra decompiler limitation)",
