      "name": "SetFpuControlWordBits",
      "signature": "ushort SetFpuControlWordBits(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ushort",
      "comment": "Modifies FPU control word bits using mask and new bit values, returns original control word.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store current FPU control word to local stack variable [EBP-0x4]\n2. Load mask parameter from stack [EBP+0x8] into EAX\n3. Copy mask to ECX for bitwise operations\n4. Apply mask to new bits parameter: EAX = wMask AND wNewBits\n5. Invert mask: ECX = NOT wMask \n6. Clear masked bits from current control word: ECX = (NOT wMask) AND currentControlWord\n7. Combine cleared control word with new masked bits: ECX = clearedBits OR maskedNewBits\n8. Store modified control word to parameter location [EBP+0xc]\n9. Load modified control word into FPU with FLDCW instruction\n10. Load original control word with sign extension to 32-bit return value\n11. Return original control word as ushort (sign-extended to int)\n\nParameters:\nwMask - Bit mask specifying which control word bits to modify (0x0000-0xFFFF)\nwNewBits - New bit values to apply where mask bits are set (0x0000-0xFFFF)\n\nReturns:\nOriginal FPU control word value before modification (0x0000-0xFFFF, sign-extended to int)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf wMask is 0x0000, no bits are modified and original control word is returned\nIf wMask is 0xFFFF, control word is completely replaced with wNewBits\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 - Offset to FPU control word storage on stack [EBP-0x4]\n0x8 - Offset to wMask parameter [EBP+0x8] \n0xc - Offset to wNewBits parameter [EBP+0xc]\n\nError Handling:\nNone - function assumes valid FPU state and parameter values\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
