      "name": "ProcessFpuTestFlags",
      "signature": "void ProcessFpuTestFlags(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Executes FPU test operations based on flag bits\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load control flags byte parameter into CL register\n2. Test bit 0 (0x01): If set, load constant from 0x1002e5b0 and store as integer\n3. Test bit 3 (0x08): If set, save FPU status word and load/store constant as double\n4. Test bit 4 (0x10): If set, load constant from 0x1002e5bc and store as double\n5. Test bit 2 (0x04): If set, load zero, load one, divide (1/0), pop stack\n6. Test bit 5 (0x20): If set, load PI constant and store as double\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nbFlags (byte): Control flags determining which FPU operations to execute\n  - Bit 0 (0x01): Execute integer store operation\n  - Bit 2 (0x04): Execute divide by zero operation\n  - Bit 3 (0x08): Execute FPU status save and constant load\n  - Bit 4 (0x10): Execute secondary constant load operation\n  - Bit 5 (0x20): Execute PI constant load operation\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function performs FPU operations but returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If no flags are set, function returns immediately after prologue\n- FPU operations may trigger floating-point exceptions based on control word\n- WAIT instructions ensure FPU operations complete before proceeding\n\nFlag Bits:\n0x01 (bit 0): Integer conversion test - loads extended double and stores as dword\n0x04 (bit 2): Division by zero test - computes 1.0/0.0 to trigger exception\n0x08 (bit 3): Status word capture - saves FPU flags and loads test constant\n0x10 (bit 4): Secondary constant test - loads from address 0x1002e5bc\n0x20 (bit 5): PI constant test - loads mathematical PI into FPU stack\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002e5b0: Primary test constant (extended double)\n0x1002e5bc: Secondary test constant (extended double)\n0x01: Integer store flag bit\n0x04: Divide by zero flag bit  \n0x08: Status capture flag bit\n0x10: Secondary constant flag bit\n0x20: PI constant flag bit",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
