      "name": "InitializeStructureWithLocale",
      "signature": "uint InitializeStructureWithLocale(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Populates a locale information structure by querying Windows locale data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer pointer (return -1 if NULL)\n2. Read primary LCID from global g_wPrimaryLcid (0x00413726)\n3. Read secondary LCID from global g_wSecondaryLcid (0x00413728)\n4. Call GetLocaleInfoByType 43 times to populate structure fields\n5. OR all return values to accumulate error flags\n6. Return combined result (0=success, non-zero=partial failure)\n\nParameters:\n  szBuffer (char*): Pointer to LocaleInfo structure (0xAC bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: 0 on complete success, -1 if buffer NULL, OR'd error flags otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers Reference (LOCALE_* constants):\n  0x31 = LOCALE_ILANGUAGE        (offset 0x04)  Language ID string\n  0x32 = LOCALE_SLANGUAGE        (offset 0x08)  Full language name\n  0x33 = LOCALE_SENGLANGUAGE     (offset 0x0C)  English language name\n  0x34 = LOCALE_SABBREVLANGNAME  (offset 0x10)  Abbreviated language name\n  0x35 = LOCALE_SNATIVELANGNAME  (offset 0x14)  Native language name\n  0x36 = LOCALE_ICOUNTRY         (offset 0x18)  Country code\n  0x37 = LOCALE_SCOUNTRY         (offset 0x00)  Full country name\n  0x2A = LOCALE_SENGCOUNTRY      (offset 0x20)  English country name\n  0x2B = LOCALE_SABBREVCTRYNAME  (offset 0x24)  Abbreviated country name\n  0x2C = LOCALE_SNATIVECTRYNAME  (offset 0x28)  Native country name\n  0x2D = LOCALE_IDEFAULTLANGUAGE (offset 0x2C)  Default language ID\n  0x2E = LOCALE_IDEFAULTCOUNTRY  (offset 0x30)  Default country code\n  0x2F = LOCALE_IDEFAULTCODEPAGE (offset 0x34)  Default OEM code page\n  0x30 = LOCALE_SLIST            (offset 0x1C)  List item separator\n  0x44 = LOCALE_IMEASURE         (offset 0x38)  Measurement system\n  0x45 = LOCALE_SDECIMAL         (offset 0x3C)  Decimal separator\n  0x46 = LOCALE_STHOUSAND        (offset 0x40)  Thousands separator\n  0x47 = LOCALE_SGROUPING        (offset 0x44)  Digit grouping\n  0x48 = LOCALE_IDIGITS          (offset 0x48)  Number of decimal digits\n  0x49 = LOCALE_ILZERO           (offset 0x4C)  Leading zeros\n  0x4A = LOCALE_SNATIVEDIGITS    (offset 0x50)  Native digit characters\n  0x4B = LOCALE_SCURRENCY        (offset 0x54)  Currency symbol\n  0x4C = LOCALE_SINTLSYMBOL      (offset 0x58)  Intl currency symbol\n  0x4D = LOCALE_SMONDECIMALSEP   (offset 0x5C)  Monetary decimal sep\n  0x4E = LOCALE_SMONTHOUSANDSEP  (offset 0x60)  Monetary thousands sep\n  0x4F = LOCALE_SMONGROUPING     (offset 0x64)  Monetary digit grouping\n  0x38 = LOCALE_ICURRDIGITS      (offset 0x68)  Currency decimal digits\n  0x39 = LOCALE_IINTLCURRDIGITS  (offset 0x6C)  Intl currency digits\n  0x3A = LOCALE_ICURRENCY        (offset 0x70)  Positive currency mode\n  0x3B = LOCALE_INEGCURR         (offset 0x74)  Negative currency mode\n  0x3C = LOCALE_SDATE            (offset 0x78)  Date separator\n  0x3D = LOCALE_STIME            (offset 0x7C)  Time separator\n  0x3E = LOCALE_SSHORTDATE       (offset 0x80)  Short date format\n  0x3F = LOCALE_SLONGDATE        (offset 0x84)  Long date format\n  0x40 = LOCALE_STIMEFORMAT      (offset 0x88)  Time format string\n  0x41 = LOCALE_IDATE            (offset 0x8C)  Short date format order\n  0x42 = LOCALE_ILDATE           (offset 0x90)  Long date format order\n  0x43 = LOCALE_ITIME            (offset 0x94)  Time format specifier\n  0x28 = LOCALE_SPOSITIVESIGN    (offset 0x98)  Positive sign\n  0x29 = LOCALE_SNEGATIVESIGN    (offset 0x9C)  Negative sign\n  0x1F = LOCALE_IPOSSIGNPOSN     (offset 0xA0)  Positive sign position\n  0x20 = LOCALE_INEGSIGNPOSN     (offset 0xA4)  Negative sign position\n  0x1003 = LOCALE_IDEFAULTANSICODEPAGE (offset 0xA8) Default ANSI codepage\n\nStructure Layout (LocaleInfo, 0xAC bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field                 Description\n  0x00    4     szCountry             Full country name ptr\n  0x04    4     szLanguageId          Language ID string ptr\n  0x08    4     szLanguageName        Full language name ptr\n  0x0C    4     szEnglishLangName     English language name ptr\n  0x10    4     szAbbrevLangName      Abbreviated lang name ptr\n  0x14    4     szNativeLangName      Native language name ptr\n  0x18    4     szCountryCode         Country code string ptr\n  0x1C    4     szListSeparator       List separator ptr\n  0x20    4     szEnglishCountry      English country name ptr\n  0x24    4     szAbbrevCountry       Abbreviated country ptr\n  0x28    4     szNativeCountry       Native country name ptr\n  0x2C    4     szDefaultLangId       Default language ID ptr\n  0x30    4     szDefaultCountry      Default country code ptr\n  0x34    4     szDefaultCodePage     Default OEM codepage ptr\n  0x38    4     szMeasure             Measurement system ptr\n  0x3C    4     szDecimalSep          Decimal separator ptr\n  0x40    4     szThousandSep         Thousands separator ptr\n  0x44    4     szGrouping            Digit grouping ptr\n  0x48    4     szDigits              Decimal digits count ptr\n  0x4C    4     szLeadingZero         Leading zeros flag ptr\n  0x50    4     szNativeDigits        Native digit chars ptr\n  0x54    4     szCurrency            Currency symbol ptr\n  0x58    4     szIntlCurrency        Intl currency symbol ptr\n  0x5C    4     szMonDecimalSep       Mon decimal sep ptr\n  0x60    4     szMonThousandSep      Mon thousands sep ptr\n  0x64    4     szMonGrouping         Mon digit grouping ptr\n  0x68    4     szCurrDigits          Currency digits ptr\n  0x6C    4     szIntlCurrDigits      Intl curr digits ptr\n  0x70    4     szCurrencyMode        Positive curr mode ptr\n  0x74    4     szNegCurrMode         Negative curr mode ptr\n  0x78    4     szDateSep             Date separator ptr\n  0x7C    4     szTimeSep             Time separator ptr\n  0x80    4     szShortDate           Short date format ptr\n  0x84    4     szLongDate            Long date format ptr\n  0x88    4     szTimeFormat          Time format ptr\n  0x8C    4     szDateOrder           Short date order ptr\n  0x90    4     szLongDateOrder       Long date order ptr\n  0x94    4     szTimeSpec            Time format spec ptr\n  0x98    4     szPositiveSign        Positive sign ptr\n  0x9C    4     szNegativeSign        Negative sign ptr\n  0xA0    4     szPosCurrSignPos      Pos sign position ptr\n  0xA4    4     szNegCurrSignPos      Neg sign position ptr\n  0xA8    4     szAnsiCodePage        ANSI codepage ptr\n\nNote: SSA variables (dwResult*, dwLocaleResult*) are EAX return value\ntemporaries from GetLocaleInfoByType calls. These are OR'd into EDI\nto track cumulative errors. They cannot be renamed as they are\nregister-based decompiler artifacts, not actual named variables.",
