      "name": "SanitizeNumericString",
      "signature": "undefined SanitizeNumericString(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sanitizes a numeric string in-place by converting ASCII digits to values and removing semicolons.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Read current character from input string\n  2. If null terminator, exit function\n  3. If character is '0'-'9' (0x30-0x39):\n     - Subtract 0x30 to convert ASCII digit to numeric value (0-9)\n     - Store result back in string, advance to next character\n  4. If character is ';' (0x3b):\n     - Remove semicolon by shifting all subsequent chars left one position\n     - Do not advance pointer (re-check same position after shift)\n  5. For any other character:\n     - Skip over it (advance pointer without modification)\n  6. Repeat from step 1\n\nParameters:\n  szInput - Pointer to null-terminated string to process (modified in-place)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; string is modified in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty string (null terminator at start): returns immediately\n  - Consecutive semicolons: each removed in sequence\n  - Non-digit, non-semicolon characters: preserved but not converted",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:17f895be47bbbb92be64950d0fefc019aed756490b2dc68a9e8aa2e6c0904fb5",
