      "name": "DeleteStructure",
      "signature": "undefined DeleteStructure(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Deletes a structure and frees its member pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if pStruct is NULL, if so return early\n  2. Load value from struct offset +0xc and compare to 0x413758 sentinel\n  3. If equal, return (already deleted or invalid)\n  4. Otherwise, free 7 member pointers from struct offsets:\n     - offset +0x10\n     - offset +0x14\n     - offset +0x18\n     - offset +0x1c\n     - offset +0x20\n     - offset +0x24\n     - offset +0x24 (end boundary marker, 0x1c bytes = 28 bytes adjusted)\n\nParameters:\n  pStruct: Pointer to structure containing allocated members\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NULL pointer check prevents crash\n  0x413758 sentinel check prevents double-deletion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
