      "name": "InitializeLocaleCharacterClassification",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeLocaleCharacterClassification(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes locale-specific character classification tables for multi-byte character set (MBCS) support.\nSets up primary and secondary character class lookup tables used by CRT character classification functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if locale initialized via g_dwLocaleFlags; if zero, reset tables to default CRT data\n  2. Query system code page info via GetLocaleInfoByType if not already cached\n  3. Allocate memory: primary table (0x202), secondary table (0x202), char buffer (0x101), wide buffer (0x202)\n  4. Initialize character buffer with ascending sequence 0x00-0xFF\n  5. Call GetCPInfo to detect multi-byte character set lead byte ranges\n  6. For MBCS (MaxCharSize > 1): mark lead byte ranges as 0x00 in character buffer\n  7. Call GetCharacterTypeInfo to populate primary character class table\n  8. Initialize wide character buffer with 0x0000-0x00FF sequence\n  9. Call ConvertWideCharToMultiByteEx to populate secondary character class table\n  10. For MBCS: mark lead byte entries with 0x8000 flag in primary table\n  11. Store table pointers in globals (g_pCharacterAttributeTable, g_pCharacterClassificationSecondary)\n  12. Free old tables if present, store new allocation addresses\n  13. Free temporary buffers and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, tables initialized\n  1 - Failure (memory allocation failed or API call failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x202 - Table size: 256 entries * 2 bytes + 2 byte header = 514 bytes\n  0x101 - Character buffer: 256 chars + null terminator = 257 bytes\n  0x100 - Character count (256 ASCII values 0x00-0xFF)\n  0x1004 - LOCALE_IDEFAULTCODEPAGE constant for GetLocaleInfo\n  0x8000 - MBCS lead byte flag marker\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pCharacterAttributeTable (0x0040ff58) - Primary class table pointer\n  g_pCharacterClassificationSecondary (0x0040ff5c) - Secondary class table pointer\n  g_pwCharClassPrimaryTable (0x00413700) - Primary allocation base for deallocation\n  g_pwCharClassSecondaryTable (0x00413704) - Secondary allocation base for deallocation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
