      "name": "ValidateLocaleEnumCallback",
      "signature": "uint ValidateLocaleEnumCallback(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "EnumSystemLocalesA callback that validates locale strings against configured codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Convert szLocaleString (hex LCID) to integer via FUN_00409cc7\n  2. Call GetLocaleInfoA with LOCALE_SISO639LANGNAME (0x1002 or 0xF007) to get language code\n  3. Compare result with g_szCountryCode (case-insensitive)\n  4. If match, set validation bits 0x304 and store LCID in g_wLocaleCodePage and g_dwLocaleId\n  5. Call GetLocaleInfoA with LOCALE_SISO3166CTRYNAME (0x1001 or 0xF003) to get country code\n  6. Compare result with g_szLocaleCode (case-insensitive)\n  7. If match and bit 0x2 not set, validate against g_dwCountryId\n  8. If country ID matches, set bit 0x2 and store LCID\n  9. If bit 0x1 not set, call FUN_00409b2a to check reserved locale list\n  10. If not reserved, set bit 0x1 and store LCID\n  11. Check if bits 0x300 are both set; if not, continue second pass\n  12. Return inverse of bit 0x4 (0 to continue enum, 1 to stop)\n\nParameters:\n  szLocaleString - Null-terminated hex string of LCID (e.g., \"00000409\" for en-US)\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE (1) to stop enumeration on failure, FALSE (0) to continue\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Flag 0xF005/0xF007 used when g_bCountryIs3Char is set (ISO 639-2 3-letter codes)\n  - Flag 0xF003/0x1001 used when g_bLocaleIs3Char is set (ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 codes)\n  - Validation bits: 0x1=locale valid, 0x2=country valid, 0x100=language match, 0x200=country match",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1210f970dd3b72dc3a9e81c331f07c265c7bf6d90b359fa5e5aae31100af7771",
