      "name": "ValidateLocaleCodepage",
      "signature": "uint ValidateLocaleCodepage(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes locale/codepage configuration from a provided locale code.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Parse locale code string to get internal ID via FUN_00409cc7\n    2. Call locale handler (g_dwLocaleHandler) to convert locale ID to codepage buffer (0x78 bytes)\n    3. If conversion fails, reset validation state to 0 and return TRUE (1)\n    4. Call FUN_0040aee0 to validate g_szLocaleCode against buffer\n    5. If validation fails and 2-char locale is expected, proceed to step 8\n    6. If validation succeeds or 3-char locale expected, call FUN_0040afb0 for country ID lookup\n    7. If lookup fails, proceed to step 8\n    8. Call FUN_00409b49 with parsed ID and result code\n    9. If FUN_00409b49 succeeds, set validation flag (bit 2) and store locale ID globally\n    10. Return success bit: ~g_dwLocaleValidation &gt;&gt; 2 &amp; 1\n\n  Parameters:\n    [EBP+0x8] szLocale - Locale code string to validate (e.g., \"enUS\", \"jaJP\")\n\n  Returns:\n    EAX - Success flag: 1 if valid, 0 if invalid/error\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - If locale handler call returns 0, immediately return success (1)\n    - 2-char vs 3-char locale detection via g_bLocaleIs3Char global\n    - Country ID validation only performed for 3-char locales when g_dwCountryId is non-NULL\n    - Global state flags updated at 0x00413744 (validation state) and 0x00413748 (locale ID)\nlpLocaleEnumProc parameter of EnumSystemLocalesA\n",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:507b5c8920efb4c518852316f7902283e0bfa1802a4cf72b2a65f7063090606f",
