      "name": "ValidateLocaleCodepageSelection",
      "signature": "undefined ValidateLocaleCodepageSelection(byte * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates a locale code (ACP or OCP) and retrieves the corresponding codepage.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Check if input is NULL or empty, or equals \"ACP\" - use code 0x1004 (ACP)\n    2. Check if input equals \"OCP\" - use code 0x000b (OCP)\n    3. If neither match, call ParseSignedInteger to parse as numeric codepage\n    4. Invoke locale handler with locale ID, codepage, and 8-byte buffer\n    5. If handler returns success, use buffer result; else use parsed parameter\n\n  Parameters:\n    szLocaleCode (ESP+4): Locale code string (\"ACP\", \"OCP\", or numeric string)\n\n  Returns:\n    int: Non-zero if locale handler succeeded, zero if failed\n\n  Structure Layout:\n    Field Offset | Size | Type | Description\n    -------------|------|------|-------------\n    szCodepageBuffer | 0xc | 8 bytes | Codepage result buffer from handler",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:16211121a6c3800a0970c44bff3ce828ad522537e29d0e2e9deba56eaddb8187",
