      "name": "ConvertIntegerToString",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertIntegerToString(int param_1, int * param_2, uint * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts an integer to its decimal string representation in a buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract digits from the integer using modulo 10 (0xa)\n  2. Store ASCII characters ('0'-'9') in buffer in reverse order\n  3. Reverse the accumulated digits to get correct order\n  4. Update buffer pointer to point past written digits\n\nParameters:\n  nValue (EAX) - Integer value to convert (may be modified during division)\n  ppBuffer (Stack+0x8) - Pointer to char* buffer pointer; updated to point after written digits\n  pCapacity (Stack+0xC) - Pointer to uint remaining buffer capacity; decremented as digits written\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies buffer and capacity in place via pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles zero by writing '0' character\n  - Stops if capacity drops below 2 (need room for digit + null terminator)\n  - Reverses digit string at end to get correct order",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
