      "name": "ConvertWideCharToMultiByteEx",
      "signature": "BOOL ConvertWideCharToMultiByteEx(DWORD param_1, LPCWSTR param_2, int param_3, LPWORD param_4, UINT param_5, LCID param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Converts wide character string to multi-byte and retrieves character type information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwLocaleInitState to determine which API path to use\n2. If state==0: Probe with GetLocaleInfoW, fallback to GetStringTypeA to detect API support\n3. If state==1: Direct call to GetLocaleInfoW for locale info retrieval\n4. If state==2: Use WideCharToMultiByte for conversion:\n   a. First pass: Query required buffer size with cbMultiByte=0\n   b. Allocate stack buffer using _alloca pattern (AllocateStackSpace)\n   c. Second pass: Perform actual conversion\n   d. Allocate char type buffer for 2x wide char count + sentinels\n   e. Call GetStringTypeA to classify converted characters\n   f. Verify sentinel markers unchanged (buffer overflow check)\n   g. Copy char type array to output via OptimizedMemoryMove\n\nParameters:\n  lcLocale (LCID) - Locale ID for locale-specific conversion\n  lpwszSource (LPCWSTR) - Source wide character string pointer\n  lpwszDest (LPWSTR) - Destination buffer for character type array\n  pdwDestLength (uint*) - Pointer to destination buffer length\n  dwCodePage (UINT) - Code page for conversion (0 uses g_dwDefaultCodePage)\n  lcLocaleForType (LCID) - Locale ID for GetStringTypeA call\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE if successful, FALSE on any API failure or buffer overflow\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - dwCodePage==0 uses default code page from g_dwDefaultCodePage\n  - Buffer overflow detected via sentinel bytes (0xFFFF) at end of char type buffer\n  - SEH exception handling for stack allocation failures\n\nDecompiler-Synthesized Variables (HASH storage, types not modifiable):\n  - pbCharTypeBuffer (byte*): Dynamically allocated character type buffer from _alloca\n  - pszMultiByteBuffer (byte*): Dynamically allocated multibyte conversion buffer from _alloca\n  Note: These use HASH storage created by decompiler for _alloca patterns.\n  The decompiler warning \"Unable to use type for symbol\" is expected behavior.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x220: WC_COMPOSITECHECK | WC_DEFAULTCHAR flags for WideCharToMultiByte\n  - 0xFFFF: Sentinel value for buffer overflow detection",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
