      "name": "ParseFileData",
      "signature": "int ParseFileData(int nHandle, DWORD dwFlags, int * pDataOut, DWORD dwSize, DWORD dwMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses binary file data by asynchronous file handle and allocates memory for parsed content.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set async file handle via SetAsyncFileHandle\n2. Validate file handle with ValidateFileHandle\n3. Allocate memory buffer (size + 0x320 bytes) for parsed file data\n4. Parse file content into allocated buffer via FUN_6f9e5775\n5. Return pointer to parsed data buffer, or NULL on allocation failure\n\nParameters:\n- nFile (int): File handle to parse (in ECX register)\n- szFilePath (char*): Path to file being parsed (source location tracking)\n- pdwFileSize (int*): Output parameter receives file size in bytes\n- szErrorFile (char*): Source code filename for error reporting\n- nLineNum (int): Source code line number for error reporting\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to parsed file data buffer, or NULL on failure",
