      "name": "SetSoundVolume",
      "signature": "undefined SetSoundVolume(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets the volume level for a sound object. Validates input, stores volume, applies global flag adjustments, and invokes audio system callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pSound pointer is non-null\n2. Store nVolume in sound structure field at offset 0xe\n3. Calculate adjusted volume using g_dwVolumeFactor scaling factor\n4. Check byte at offset 0xd & 0x04; if set and GetGlobalFlag() == 2, use adjusted volume\n5. If g_dwSoundMute is set, override to 0\n6. Call Ordinal_10054 with clipped volume (0.0-255.0)\n7. Call sound object virtual method at offset 0x3c with computed volume\n\nParameters:\n- pSound (void*): Sound object pointer; must be non-null\n- nVolume (int): Desired volume level (0-255 range)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xe: Offset in sound structure for volume storage\n- 0xd: Offset in sound structure for flags byte\n- 0x04: Flag bit mask (controls volume adjustment behavior)\n- 0xff: Volume scaling divisor\n- 0x3c: Offset to volume update method in vtable\n- 2: Global flag value for volume adjustment",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
