      "name": "ComputeFloatRemainderWithExceptionHandling",
      "signature": "undefined4 ComputeFloatRemainderWithExceptionHandling(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Computes the IEEE 754 floating-point remainder with exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input double has NaN/infinity exponent (0x7ff mask)\n2. If NaN/infinity: divide to propagate exception and return\n3. Check FPU status word for pending exceptions (bits 11-13)\n4. If exceptions pending: call extended precision division handler\n5. Otherwise: save ST(1) to stack, perform division, restore\n\nParameters:\n  dwDoubleLow  - Low 32 bits of the double dividend (in_ST0) [Stack+0x4]\n  dwDoubleHigh - High 32 bits of the double dividend [Stack+0x8]\n  IMPLICIT: ST(0) - First floating-point operand (dividend)\n  IMPLICIT: ST(1) - Second floating-point operand (divisor)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Unused (stack cleanup placeholder)\n  ST(0) - Remainder result after division\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NaN/Infinity: If exponent bits == 0x7ff00000, propagates NaN by performing FDIV\n  FPU Exceptions: Bits 0x3800 in FPU status word indicate precision/underflow/overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7ff00000 - IEEE 754 double exponent mask for NaN/infinity detection\n  0x3800     - FPU status word mask: bits 11(OE), 12(UE), 13(PE)\n\nAssembly-Only Variables:\n  local_10 (Stack[-0x10]:10) - Extended precision float10 temporary for ST(1) preservation",
