      "name": "DivideFloatSafe",
      "signature": "undefined4 DivideFloatSafe(uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs safe floating-point division with special value handling.\n\nClassification: Worker - Handles float division with INF/NaN edge cases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent bits from flDivisor (mask 0x7f800000)\n2. If exponent == 0x7f800000 (INF/NaN): perform direct FDIVR and return\n3. Check FPU status word for stack non-empty (mask 0x3800)\n4. If FPU stack has values: call PrepareExtendedDivisionOperands with current state\n5. Otherwise: save ST0 to stack, load flDivisor, call helper, restore ST0\n\nParameters:\n  flDivisor (float): The divisor value for division operation\n  IMPLICIT ST0 (float10): Dividend value in FPU register ST0\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result left in ST0 after division (ST0 / flDivisor)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - INF divisor: Fast path via FDIVR (0x10020c30)\n  - NaN divisor: Fast path via FDIVR (0x10020c30)\n  - FPU stack active: Marshals to extended precision division\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7f800000 - IEEE 754 single-precision exponent mask (all 1s = INF/NaN)\n  0x3800     - FPU status word TOP field mask (stack pointer bits)\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  local_10 (Stack[-0x10]:10): Temporary storage for ST0 spill (float10)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
