      "name": "ComputeExtendedRemainderCore",
      "signature": "float10 ComputeExtendedRemainderCore(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10",
      "comment": "Core algorithm for computing extended precision (80-bit) floating-point remainder.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDX and allocate 0x30 bytes for FPU operand storage\n2. Store ST0 (dividend) and ST1 (divisor) as extended doubles to stack\n3. Extract exponent from dividend mantissa high bits\n4. If exponent is zero (denormalized), jump to FPREM fast path\n5. Otherwise, call ComputeExtendedFloatRemainder for iterative computation\n6. For zero divisor case, use hardware FPREM instruction directly\n7. Restore stack and return result in ST0\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_ST0 [float10] - Dividend extended precision float\n  IMPLICIT in_ST1 [float10] - Divisor extended precision float\n\nReturns:\n  float10 in ST0 - Partial remainder of dividend / divisor\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero exponent: Uses FPREM hardware instruction at 0x10020fc7\n  - Valid exponent: Delegates to ComputeExtendedFloatRemainder at 0x10020d16\n  - Zero divisor mantissa: Fast path via FPREM\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7fff0000 - Exponent mask for normalized float check\n  0x30       - Stack allocation for two 10-byte floats + control words\n\nStructure Layout (Stack Frame):\n  Offset  Size  Field            Type      Description\n  0x00    10    ldDivisor        float10   First FPU operand (divisor)\n  0x0C    10    temp1            float10   Temporary for scaled values\n  0x18    10    ldDividend       float10   Second FPU operand (dividend)\n  0x24    2     wFPUControlSave  ushort    Saved FPU control word\n  0x28    4     dwTempControl    uint      Modified control word",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
      "method": "NOP",
