      "name": "ComputeExtendedRemainderCore",
      "signature": "undefined4 ComputeExtendedRemainderCore(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2, ushort param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Computes partial remainder of two 80-bit extended precision floating-point numbers.\n\nThis is the core implementation of x87 FPREM/FPREM1 instruction emulation for\nextended precision (80-bit) floats. It handles the iterative subtraction\nalgorithm required when exponent difference exceeds hardware capabilities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate operands - check for special cases (NaN, infinity, denormals)\n2. Extract and compare exponents of dividend and divisor\n3. If exponent difference > 63: use iterative scaled subtraction loop\n4. If exponent difference <= 63: use FPREM hardware instruction directly\n5. Apply sign from original dividend to result\n\nParameters:\n  dwMantissaLo     - Low 32 bits of dividend mantissa (bits 0-31)\n  dwMantissaHiAndExp - High 32 bits containing mantissa bits 32-47 and partial exponent\n  wSignExp         - Sign bit (bit 15) and exponent (bits 0-14) of dividend\n  IMPLICIT: Second operand (divisor) passed at [ESP+0x1C] to [ESP+0x24] (10 bytes)\n  IMPLICIT: Result written to [ESP+0x28] to [ESP+0x31] (10 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX preserved from entry (return value not meaningful)\n  Result in ST0 and memory at [ESP+0x28]\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns unchanged if divisor exponent is 0 (denormal/zero)\n  - Returns unchanged if divisor exponent is 0x7FFF (infinity/NaN)\n  - Returns unchanged if dividend exponent is 0x7FFF (infinity/NaN)\n  - Uses scaled subtraction when exponents differ by more than 63\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7FFF - Maximum biased exponent for extended precision (infinity/NaN marker)\n  0x8000 - Sign bit mask for 80-bit extended float\n  0x7800 - Exponent field mask for normalization table lookup\n  0x700  - Exponent bits used for special case detection\n  0x3F   - Maximum reduction per iteration (63 bits)\n  0x20   - Minimum iterations mask (32)\n\nStructure Layout (80-bit Extended Precision):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Type    Description\n  0x00    4     Mantissa Lo    uint    Bits 0-31 of 64-bit mantissa\n  0x04    2     Mantissa Hi    ushort  Bits 32-47 of 64-bit mantissa  \n  0x06    2     Mantissa Top   ushort  Bits 48-63 of 64-bit mantissa\n  0x08    2     SignExp        ushort  Bit 15=sign, bits 0-14=biased exponent",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2dae5d25661498efe8fa4629cf9d60a27aecd92f505583609fbbb2b465523d9b",
