      "name": "ComputeExtendedRemainderEntry",
      "signature": "float10 ComputeExtendedRemainderEntry(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10",
      "comment": "Entry point for extended precision floating-point remainder computation.\n\nPrepares operands and delegates to ComputeExtendedRemainderCore for the main algorithm.\nHandles cases where operands need scaling before remainder calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract dividend mantissa high bits and exponent from ST1\n2. Check if dividend exponent is normalized (non-zero in 0x7FFF0000 mask)\n3. If normalized: call ComputeExtendedRemainderCore directly\n4. If denormalized: scale both operands by 2^64 before processing\n5. If divisor is zero/very small: compute remainder using FPREM directly\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_ST0 - Dividend (float10) passed in x87 FPU register ST(0)\n  IMPLICIT in_ST1 - Divisor (float10) passed in x87 FPU register ST(1)\n\nReturns:\n  float10 in ST(0) - The partial remainder of dividend/divisor\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Normalized exponents: Direct call to core algorithm\n  - Denormalized operands: Scaled by g_dExponentScaleFactor (2^64) before processing\n  - Zero/near-zero divisor: Uses FPREM hardware instruction at 0x10021282\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7fff0000 - Exponent field mask for normalized float check\n  2^64       - Scale factor for denormalized operands (g_dExponentScaleFactor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
