      "name": "ComputePowerWithCPUCheck",
      "signature": "double ComputePowerWithCPUCheck(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "double",
      "comment": "Computes base^exponent using x87 FPU with CPU capability checks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if DAT_6fc468fc flag is set (CPU capability enabled)\n2. If flag is zero, skip to standard pow() path\n3. If flag is set, verify MXCSR flags equal 0x1f80 (SSE/AVX enabled)\n4. If MXCSR check fails, skip to standard pow() path\n5. Verify FPU control word masked to 0x7f equals 0x7f (all precision enabled)\n6. If FPU check fails, skip to standard pow() path\n7. If all CPU checks pass, call ComputePowerFunctionFPUWrapper at 0x6fc2db30\n8. If any check fails, call standard pow() function with double conversion\n\nParameters:\nST0 (implicit) - Exponent value (float10)\nST1 (implicit) - Base value (float10)\nin_FPUControlWord - FPU control word register from FNSTCW instruction\nMXCSR - SSE control/status register\n\nReturns:\nST0 (float10) - Result of base^exponent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fc468fc: Flag at 0x6fc468fc controls which implementation to use\n- MXCSR mask 0x1f80: Verifies SSE denormal mode, rounding, precision flags\n- FPU control mask 0x7f: Checks FPU exception masks and precision mode\n- All checks must pass to use wrapper; any failure falls back to pow()\n- Wrapper function provides custom x87 optimization for power computation\n- Standard path converts float10 to double, calls pow(), converts back",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
