      "name": "DispatchExtendedPrecisionFloatOperation",
      "signature": "float10 * DispatchExtendedPrecisionFloatOperation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Table-driven dispatcher for extended-precision floating-point operations on 80-bit values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2c (44) bytes of stack space for local extended-precision values\n2. Extract all 8 FPU registers (ST0-ST7) and decompose each into components (low 32-bit, high 32-bit, 16-bit exponent)\n3. Mask EAX opcode selector to 6 bits (0-63) for safe table indexing\n4. Jump to appropriate handler via table at 0x6ff8005e using (opcodeSelector * 4) as offset\n5. Execute selected operation (simple FPU ops, calls to ExtendedPrecisionFloatDivide, or INT 6 for invalid cases)\n6. Return result in ST0 register (80-bit extended precision float)\n\nParameters:\n- opcodeSelector (EAX): Operation type selector (0-63); masked with 0x3f before dispatch\n- ST0-ST7: Input extended-precision floating-point operands (80-bit each)\n\nReturns:\n- ST0: Result of selected operation (may be final result, NaN, or intermediate value)\n- Stack frame restored (0x2c bytes deallocated)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Opcodes 0,2,4,6,14,16,1E,26,2E,36,3E: Return value computed from ST0/ST0 division (produces NaN)\n- Opcodes 1,3,9,11,13,1B,23,2B,33,3B: Trigger INT 6 (software interrupt for invalid operations)\n- Remaining opcodes: Call ExtendedPrecisionFloatDivide with various register pair combinations\n- Jump table is compact (64 entries * 4 bytes = 256 bytes) at 0x6ff8005e\n- Function uses __stdcall convention: callee cleans up stack",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
