      "name": "InitializeFloatingPointExceptions",
      "signature": "void InitializeFloatingPointExceptions(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes floating-point exception handling by loading special FPU values and exception handlers based on control flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX register and allocate 8 bytes temporary storage on stack\n2. Load fpExceptionFlags parameter from stack into CL register\n3. If bit 0x01 set: Load extended double from g_extendedFpuValue1, convert to integer, store in stack\n4. If bit 0x08 set: Load extended double from g_extendedFpuValue1, store as double on stack\n5. If bit 0x10 set: Load extended double from g_extendedFpuValue2, store as double on stack\n6. If bit 0x04 set: Generate infinity value (1.0/0.0) and pop from FPU stack\n7. If bit 0x20 set: Load pi constant (FLDPI), store as double on stack\n8. Pop temporary storage and return to caller\n\nParameters:\nfpExceptionFlags (uchar): Control flags byte with bits indicating which FPU exception values to initialize:\n  - Bit 0x01: Load and convert extended value from g_extendedFpuValue1 to integer\n  - Bit 0x04: Generate infinity value (IEEE 754 division by zero)\n  - Bit 0x08: Load extended value from g_extendedFpuValue1 as double\n  - Bit 0x10: Load extended value from g_extendedFpuValue2 as double\n  - Bit 0x20: Load pi constant (FLDPI)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Does not return a value. Initializes FPU stack with exception handler values.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic values:\n  - g_extendedFpuValue1 (0x6fc42188): Extended double precision value (12 bytes)\n  - g_extendedFpuValue2 (0x6fc42194): Extended double precision value (12 bytes)\n  \nFPU behavior:\n  - Infinity calculation uses IEEE 754 division by zero which triggers FPU exception\n  - WAIT instruction after each FSTP ensures FPU operation completes before next instruction\n  - Stack allocation: Two PUSH ECX allocates 8 bytes for temporary FPU operand storage\n  - FPU stack manipulation: Function leaves values on FPU stack for caller to use\n  - Calling functions must manage FPU state and clean up stack after exception handling\n\nImplementation notes:\n  - Part of runtime floating-point exception initialization or signal handler setup\n  - Used in exception handling path to initialize special IEEE 754 values (infinity, pi)\n  - Multiple conditional branches allow selective initialization based on flags\n  - Called from __handle_exc exception handler function",
